  "description": "Grilled corn is slathered with a harissa-spiked compound butter for a quick, flavorful side that's smoky, spicy, and perfect for summer.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: harissa paste → more to taste\n\nNotes: This recipe can easily be doubled.\nFor best results, look for a mild-to-medium-spicy harissa to balance heat without overpowering the other flavors. I recommend mild harissa and prefer the brand Mina.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The compound butter can be prepared ahead and refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 1 week.",
